uish access as soon as you finish using the resource. Call the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/NSURL\/stopAccessingSecurityScopedResource()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method to relinquish access. You must balance each call to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/NSURL\/startAccessingSecurityScopedResource()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a given security-scoped URL with a call to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/NSURL\/stopAccessingSecurityScopedResource()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". When you make the last balanced call to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentation\/Foundation\/NSURL\/stopAccessingSecurityScopedResource()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", you immediately lose access to the resource in question.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If you fail to relinquish your access to file-system resources when you no longer need them, your app leaks kernel resources. If sufficient kernel resources leak, your app loses its ability to add file-system locations to its sandbox, such as with Powerbox or security-scoped bookmarks, until relaunched.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Warning","style":"warning","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Security-scoped bookmarks aren’t available in versions of macOS prior to OS X 10.7.3.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Version note","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Working-with-Bookmark-Data","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.foundation\/documentatio